-- new `SimulationCore::restore_from_snapshot()`, `ImpactDamageModel::restore_from_snapshot()`, and `ManipulatorRig::restore_from_snapshot()` factories that reconstruct already-validated state (rejecting non-finite/out-of-range physical, energy, and thermal parameters, capacity/allocation contradictions, `is_scanning`/`active_scan_target_id` disagreement, and manipulator poses no live command sequence could reach) without replaying gameplay-command side effects, plus a `DamageAwareProbeRuntime::restore_from_snapshot()` composing the first two; static bodies, policy, and target selection are restored afterward through the same validated mutators live gameplay already uses (`add_static_sphere_body`, `install_policy`, `select_target`) rather than a parallel unvalidated path. Restoring a persisted contact also restores `ImpactDamageModel`'s internal assessment watermark, so a contact already baked into the saved integrity is not charged against it again on the first tick after loading;
-- `capture_probe_save_data()` / `restore_probe_runtime()` / `restore_manipulator_rig()` bridge functions and `serialize_save_game()` / `deserialize_save_game()` round-trip the whole schema to/from human-inspectable JSON text.
